# ## HANDOFF CONSTRUCTION (Cline ↔ OpenCode)
#
# When delegating to an OpenCode agent, use inline context delivery (D216 mandate):
#
# ```python
# hivemind_submit_handoff(
#     source="cline/omega-engine",
#     target="opencode/<entity>",   # kali, maat, lilith, doom_guy, jem, verity, researcher, roc_racoon
#     priority=0|1|2,               # 0=normal, 1=high, 2=critical
#     task="<one-line description>",
#     context="""<INLINE context per D216 — file paths alone are unreliable>""",
#     expected_output="<file path, schema, or report>",
#     relevant_files=["<paths>"]
# )
# ```
#
# **D216 Mandate**: All context MUST be embedded inline in prompt text.
# File paths are supplementary only — subagents cannot reliably read files.
#
